  "conclusion": {
    "points": [
      "The incidence and necessity for surgical decortication has decreased due to fibrinolysis strategies, especially in stage I–II empyema.",
      "Patients referred for surgery are increasingly those with advanced stage III–IV empyema or who failed intrapleural fibrinolysis.",
      "VATS should be first-line surgical approach when feasible.",
      "Integration of risk stratification (RAPID) and ERAS protocols improves outcomes and reduces complications."
    ],
    "reference": "[Chapter Conclusion]"
